BT /F1 13.00 Tf 0.1216 0.2275 0.3725 rg 56.693 473.386 Td (Steps) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 450.709 Td (1. Print and check the 3 cm calibration square before cutting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 428.031 Td (2. This block uses standard assumptions for shoulder slope, underbust and arm width  sew a quick muslin) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 412.157 Td (\(test version\) from cheap fabric first and adjust before cutting your real fabric.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 389.480 Td (3. Cut every piece as labelled: pieces marked 'on fold' on the fabric fold, 'cut 2' twice, sleeves twice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 366.803 Td (4. Fuse interfacing to the neck facings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 344.126 Td (5. Staystitch the neckline just inside the seam line so it doesn't stretch while you work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 321.449 Td (6. Staystitch the curved princess edges too, for the same reason.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 298.772 Td (7. Sew each bodice princess seam: pin center panel to side panel matching the bust notch, sew, clip the side) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 282.898 Td (panel's curve over the bust inside the seam allowance, press toward the center.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 260.220 Td (8. Sew the remaining waist darts \(where a panel wasn't split\), pressing toward the center.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 237.543 Td (9. Sew the bodice shoulder seams and press them open.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 214.866 Td (10. Sew the front and back neck facings together at the shoulders; finish the facing's outer edge \(zigzag,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 198.992 Td (overlock or turn 5 mm and stitch\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 176.315 Td (11. Attach the facing to the neckline right sides together, leaving the last 2 cm free at each center back edge) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 160.441 Td (\(the zipper goes there later\). Trim to 6 mm, clip into the curve every 2 cm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 137.764 Td (12. Understitch: press the seam allowance toward the facing and stitch it to the facing 2 mm from the seam ) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 121.890 Td (this keeps the facing rolled inside. Turn, press, tack at the shoulder seams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 99.213 Td (13. Sew the bodice side seams.) Tj ET

